check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9346760Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9356580Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9449239Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9458091Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9458632Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9459339Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9459622Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9460009Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9460650Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9461046Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9461334Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9462319Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9462607Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9463073Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9464182Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9464802Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9465278Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9465506Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9465796Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9466144Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9466411Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9466901Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9467186Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9467326Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9467553Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9467966Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9471893Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9472116Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9472205Z I will:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9472572Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9473047Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9473595Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9474286Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9474640Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9474892Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9475150Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9475509Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9475838Z    /root
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9484846Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9485302Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9496091Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9496572Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9496900Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9498195Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:16.9498656Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
