composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:24.8585209Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:24.8586066Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:24.8587111Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:24.8588000Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:24.8588391Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:24.8588574Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:24.8588784Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:24.8589056Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:24.8589294Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:24.8589705Z    can use Nix.
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:24.8589858Z 
composition-native (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:24.8589975Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
