check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2443059Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2450137Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2538411Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2547922Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2548825Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2549563Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2549849Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2550136Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2550721Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2551155Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2551879Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2552507Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2553088Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2553653Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2554313Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2554883Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2555469Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2555685Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2555980Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2556276Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2556585Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2557153Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2557367Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2557510Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2557802Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2558484Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2559190Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2559469Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2559723Z I will:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2559990Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2560244Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2560752Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2561383Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2561892Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2562276Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2562769Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2563268Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2563873Z    /root
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2573154Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2573876Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2582815Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2583447Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2583779Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2584302Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2584853Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2601400Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2602599Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2611540Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2612392Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2614652Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2615007Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2615215Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2615540Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2615756Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2616402Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2616802Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2616973Z If you would like to
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2617384Z see the output, try like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2617632Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2617916Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2618650Z   $ sh ./install-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2619003Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2619018Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T03:05:45.2619396Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
